{"title":"2013 AIME II Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose that the measurement of time during the day is converted to the metric system so that each day has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> metric hours, and each metric hour has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> metric minutes. Digital clocks would then be produced that would read <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/d/a9d6c4c894675e5b477cb841941f1e76fa819541.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{9:99}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"13\" /> just before midnight, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/d/0cdf4445c20917765b953ade80435c3be8abadee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{0:00}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> at midnight, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/5/245ad26fd6c0dea1c29919b39a7a25de0ecb4b65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{1:25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> at the former <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/d/cad4817a5db25357324185a3c29c18e1641cc88e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{3:00}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> AM, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/0/f4049f541675fbbe9d6cfbfa075909a7406b380c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{7:50}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> at the former <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/c/f4c9157dead541e813164bf466e2e94f6a74fda5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{6:00}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> PM. After the conversion, a person who wanted to wake up at the equivalent of the former <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/0/9a07dad3fc95afbd4f73bdeeb532bac1c3a0fe1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{6:36}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> AM would set his new digital alarm clock for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/b/a4b2575cabc9b22b5532709c8f9138e7f52ea8e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{A:BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/4/7c43070a2acf8f4e25d98e48c404d9348a26d40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/9/09920c3af0daa12ac2ec5174e737c31e0f8cec75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{B}$\" width=\"11\" height=\"11\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/0/aa04d7a9bcbf1fe3f2037cbc5e763c4b6d2661d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"13\" /> are digits. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/a/52aa801c37e61c70150a039eea8bb3e7da75329f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100\\text{A}+10\\text{B}+\\text{C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"125\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/1/b11ab1bdea9a307bf7c59def9ad8bfe9168103e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24 \\cdot 60=1440$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"112\" height=\"14\" /> normal minutes in a day , and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/c/62c7d1fb6940d57d5a8b6d0f6e5f81b74d73b842.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10 \\cdot 100=1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"121\" height=\"14\" /> metric minutes in a day. The ratio of normal to metric minutes in a day is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/1/7513d3cd6ed3fc452324789e42727c6d64666b47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1440}{1000}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"38\" height=\"38\" />, which simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/a/bda4c8e3a73638d0618ce2f5af51e7113dda3535.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{36}{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />. This means that every time 36 normal minutes pass, 25 metric minutes pass. From midnight to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/0/9a07dad3fc95afbd4f73bdeeb532bac1c3a0fe1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{6:36}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> AM, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b2376880ce53a6a8e816c3d13ff0b8ff5d2d0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 \\cdot 60+36=396$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"134\" height=\"15\" /> normal minutes pass. This can be viewed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/3/c53fb24ed3fbf867c31a4e9eadc3742cf5269df5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{396}{36}=11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"72\" height=\"37\" /> cycles of 36 normal minutes, so 11 cycles of 25 metric minutes pass. Adding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/d/24d2ec52ca44cef4f46d9b0b9f52c7c47d8db87a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25 \\cdot 11=275$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"103\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/d/0cdf4445c20917765b953ade80435c3be8abadee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{0:00}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/a/1cace06a8f3096f3bc03ac576c00bd14af6fb879.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{2:75}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/c/cdca8d1bc480bece31d161023a38f66d9075fc97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{275}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First we want to find out what fraction of a day has passed at 6:36 AM. One hour is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/1/c51114e934665d550355149cfcd5ac930b13606b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{24}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" /> of a day, and 36 minutes is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/8/138a35cf69a8ea4aa2af04b777b15025255e48ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{36}{60}=\\frac{3}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"58\" height=\"37\" /> of an hour, so at 6:36 AM, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/8/9a89a3f8fa00120a97b130e1927499f1efbd08d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 \\cdot \\frac{1}{24} + \\frac{1}{24} \\cdot \\frac{3}{5}=\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{1}{40}=\\frac{11}{40}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"241\" height=\"38\" /> of a day has passed. Now the metric timing equivalent of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/8/8f86a51e784c11ee9485dc6b82eb808de41ed22d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{11}{40}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" /> of a day is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/4/a943daad6a057c46d67fe6e06c47428927480626.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{11}{40}\\cdot 1000=275$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"125\" height=\"38\" /> metric minutes, which is equivalent to 2 metric hours and 75 metric minutes, so our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/c/cdca8d1bc480bece31d161023a38f66d9075fc97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{275}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" /> - mathleticguyyy\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II\" title=\"2013 AIME II\">2013 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2013 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2013 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2013\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Problem</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2013 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2013 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2013 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2013 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2013 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2013 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2013 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2013 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2013 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2013 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2013 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2013 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2013 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2013 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2013 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017140245\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.034 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.050 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 229/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1774/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 133/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpens